the line that passes through the points $H(1,-2,3)$ and $S(4,-2,1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492050 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ba6720d7-134d-5884-b22f-7f4012ec3a77" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492050 #edb/ref 1074 "The vector equation of the straight line passing through $H$ and parallel to $v$ is given by\n\n$$\nr=h+tv,\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$ and $h$ is the position vector of $H.$ \n\nWe can find a direction vector by computing the displacement vector between the given points $H(1,-2,3)$ and $S(4,-2,1),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{HS} \\\\  & =⟨4,-2,1⟩-⟨1,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,0,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector equation of the line is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492072 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186491919 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492072 #edb/ref 1069 "q-69799" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492072 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492072 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the straight line that passes through $P(-4,2,-3)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩.$ Find all the possible points $X$ on that line such that $XP=\\sqrt{20}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492072 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fae33bcb-2652-544e-838d-9fea7f4029a9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492072 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the vector equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =⟨-4,\\,2,\\,-3⟩+t⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSince $X$ lies on the line, we know that there must be a real number $t$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OX} & =⟨-4,\\,2,\\,-3⟩+t⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PX} & =\\overset{\\to }{OX}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =(⟨-4,\\,2,\\,-3⟩+t⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩)-⟨-4,\\,2,\\,-3⟩ \\\\  & =t⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $PX=\\sqrt{20},$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XP & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\ |\\overset{\\to }{PX}| & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\ |⟨t,\\,0,\\,2t⟩| & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\ \\sqrt{{t}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(2t)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\ \\sqrt{5{t}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\ \\pm \\sqrt{5}t & =2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ t & =\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, putting the values $t=\\pm 2$ into the equation for the line, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{O{X}_{1}}=⟨-4,\\,2,\\,-3⟩+2⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩=⟨-2,2,1⟩, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{O{X}_{2}}=⟨-4,\\,2,\\,-3⟩-2⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩=⟨-6,2,-7⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the points are ${X}_{1}(-2,2,1)$ and ${X}_{2}(-6,2,-7).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492082 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186492093 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492082 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1ec7ec1f-8794-50d0-a0c9-c532caebad39" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492082 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186492050 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492089 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186492082 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492089 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3b25e9df-26b3-594e-b7e5-ee4df36a2c1f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492089 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186492072 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492093 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186492111 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492093 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4cb265da-0c2e-574b-9b97-7e10561660e5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492093 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186106066 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492105 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186492089 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492105 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bb116c13-04f6-5718-b5fc-2b6fa8103e9e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492105 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186106283 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492111 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fa1f6cbe-7cdd-5cc9-a956-7908cb978446" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186492111 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186281392 #edb/ref 175921860